framework DecisionAnalysis:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain A3B8IntegratedStage:
  description "Audited plan for one combined A3 and B8 Stage candidate without schema-3 activation or production promotion."

problem P1:
  |
    Prepare the owner-approved combined A3 and B8 Stage candidate so the exact
    deployed revision can prove corrected V2 new-character creation and strict
    V2/V3 generation reads before any schema-3 policy selection or production
    migration. Keep provider work, pointer movement and production promotion
    inside their separate authority boundaries.

premise AUTHORITY:
  |
    The owner approved proceeding with one combined A3 and B8 Stage candidate
    after being shown that a narrow A3-only release was not the global optimum.
    Accepted ADR-0030 and requirement revision 6 preserve immutable generations,
    version-qualified contracts, no read-time provider calls, and separate
    provider, pointer, policy, rollback and production-promotion effects.

evidence E_CURRENT:
  |
    The current branch contains the corrected V2 authoring response grammar,
    the V3 migration contracts and persistence, and the focused semantic
    authoring kernel. The public create route still targets V2. The current
    character asset repository parses only V2 envelopes, while generic asset
    storage can retain schema-versioned V2 and V3 generations.

evidence E_STAGE:
  |
    The Stage workflow deploys an exact tagged Cloud Run revision without
    traffic, applies forward-only migrations, builds an immutable Worker
    preview, and runs temporary authenticated smoke data with cleanup. Its
    existing smoke proves one retained V2 read but neither an exact V3 read nor
    migration-work resume, and it does not exercise character creation.

evidence E_PROVIDER_BOUND:
  |
    For an empty temporary owner and a prompt that requests no relationship,
    the create path has one initial generation logical call, one definition
    call plus at most one schema-repair call, one definition review, one profile
    generation and one profile validation. Each logical call can contact at
    most three configured real providers in order; two can fail once as
    unavailable and the last can make at most three same-provider attempts.
    Therefore one client create request has a conservative hard maximum of
    thirty provider HTTP attempts. Actual dollar cost is not fixed by code.

premise ALTERNATIVES:
  |
    A deploy the branch and infer compatibility from local tests. B enable V3
    current selection and battle binding now. C add an exact version-dispatched
    generation reader plus Stage-only temporary V2/V3 and migration-resume
    probes, while leaving current selection and schema policy unchanged; add a
    separately enabled one-request A3 create smoke and require explicit numeric
    paid-run review immediately before dispatch.

pending U1:
  |
    The exact paid dollar amount for the A3 create smoke cannot be guaranteed
    because provider choice, token use, repair and retry outcomes vary. The
    operation ceiling and observed result must be reported separately.

pending U2:
  |
    Merge, release-tag creation and Stage workflow dispatch remain concrete
    external writes. Re-read exact revision, required checks and owner authority
    before each; production promotion is excluded.

decision D1 based_on P1, AUTHORITY, E_CURRENT, E_STAGE, E_PROVIDER_BOUND, ALTERNATIVES, U1, U2:
  |
    Choose C. First add and test a strict exact-generation reader that dispatches
    only on matching storage and envelope versions 2 or 3, validates content
    digest and version-specific contracts, derives a public legacy-shaped sheet,
    and compiles the qualified V3 semantic programs without changing any current
    pointer or readiness policy. Extend the temporary authenticated Stage smoke
    to prove historical V2 read, non-current V3 read, mixed-tuple rejection,
    migration attempt load/resume and cleanup with zero provider calls. Add an
    opt-in A3 API create smoke that makes one client request, polls one attempt,
    verifies a corrected V2 candidate, discards it and relies on owner deletion
    for cleanup. Run focused and full local gates, then prepare a reviewable PR.
    Before any paid A3 dispatch, present the thirty-attempt ceiling, cost
    uncertainty and cleanup behavior for an exact decision. Do not activate
    schema 3, move a production character pointer, accept a generated candidate,
    promote production or silently include another release effect.
